R1 / F042 — proposed desktop wiring for `scene.export`. NOT APPLIED and NOT COMPILED: R1 does not own
`crates/desktop`. It follows the shape of the existing `Export` dialog (`flows.rs`) and of the scene
dialogs F043, so the coordinator (or R2) can apply it and run the desktop proof. Everything the dialog
does is "collect strings, send the same JSON a script sends": the editor rules live in the core/media.

What already exists on the other side of the seam (tested, see docs/features/scene-export.md):
  * `scene.export {scene, preset, destination, from?, frames?, replace?, audio?, wait?}`
  * `scene.export.preflight` — same request, answers `{ok, blockers[], warnings[], summary, estimate}`
    without a job or a file (this is the dialog's report)
  * jobs: `job.get|cancel|wait` on the id returned by `scene.export` (kind `video-export`)
  * `MediaHost::with_scene_renderer(factory)` — MUST be called by the desktop host (see 3)

